{"agent":"Monster3-MX-suite-waste-report-7267fe","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"`_is_suite` treats any standalone `tests` or `tests/` token in a `unit_tests` command as proof that the whole suite ran, so commands that explicitly exclude the tests directory are misclassified as whole-suite runs. For example, given one real whole-suite run `pytest tests/` on a clean tree and a later `unit_tests` event on the same clean tree with command `pytest --ignore tests/`, `_is_suite` returns `True` for the second event, `classify` puts it in `rerun_same_tree_other_item`, and `build` reports an avoidable share of `1/2`. The second command does not run the whole `tests/` directory, so it should not be in `runs` at all; the correct report for that input has `runs=1`, `avoidable=0`, and `avoidable_share=0`.","digest":"130dbcea86ebf621","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/perf/suitewaste.py:_is_suite","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/perf/suitewaste.py:_is_suite"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`_minutes` returns a partial sum when some per-run values are missing, silently reporting an incomplete class total as if it were the figure. For example, a class containing one run with `elapsed_s=600` and one run with `elapsed_s` absent gets `suite_minutes=10.0` instead of `None` with an `unavailable` explanation. The module contract says a figure the log cannot give is `None` with a reason, but this input produces a non-`None` class minutes figure that cannot be trusted as the total.","digest":"2764c3861329b798","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/perf/suitewaste.py:_minutes","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/perf/suitewaste.py:_minutes"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"A phase-scoped suitewaste query is classified against the whole log. The handler rejects an unknown phase, then calls `SW.build(events, cfg, now, probes, since=floor)` and never passes `phase`, while `swarm` on the same path does filter. Given events where phase `a` has only unavoidable whole-suite runs and phase `b` has avoidable ones, `metrics` view `suitewaste` with phase `a` still folds `b` into the avoidable share (and the reason breakdown), so the figure is not the phase the caller asked for.","digest":"a5167f662f2261fc","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/metrics/service.py:_own_fold","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/metrics/service.py:_own_fold"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`seen` stores only the first item that covered a code tree, so a later rework by another item is not classed as a same-item rerun. Given lane-b then lane-a then lane-a again on tree key K, the third run is `rerun_same_tree_other_item` because `seen[K]` is still lane-b. The module contract says a rerun is same-item when an earlier run of that tree was by the same item, so that input is `rerun_same_tree_same_item`.","digest":"106d27bfdcb1a664","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/perf/suitewaste.py:131","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/perf/suitewaste.py:131"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"Unplaced runs are unknown, but they still sit in the avoidable-share denominator and can refute the falsifier. With minimum 1, one `rerun_same_tree_same_item` and four `unplaced` rows give `avoidable_share` 0.2 and `falsifier.holds` false (`REFUTED`), even though those four name no tree git can read and the only placed run was avoidable. The claim “under 25 percent avoidable” is not shown; the unknowns are treated as non-avoidable.","digest":"6c51db2be8e09768","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/perf/suitewaste.py:191","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/perf/suitewaste.py:191"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":24887,"diff_sha":"2644bfe5e7c295d567d9b5d7bdd7a12965921f9b4a0ee96e089d07fb12a7cb02","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/MX-suite-waste-report","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":0.9,"excluded_bytes":4633,"excluded_files":3,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr"],"family":"alibaba","findings":5,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"dcfb062a77e64dd3","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/MX-suite-waste-report.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261112T121645Z-171c5e07.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_for_holder":"[REDACTED:hostname]-MX-suite-waste-report-7267fe reviewed lane-sl-throughput's MX-suite-waste-report","reviewed_head":"ea05dc5da3f23a1dfc217835ed45e00be6490a4d","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 18fb2b9d589c28fed408628b4ec103d6021e1ef6","ddflow/api/metrics.py":"100644 b9fc9ade5417cbafa75893d5fbdbe2a7c3e66411","ddflow/core/metrics.py":"100644 14713f224cffce2ed60f650099aa0e6fd4e0bd0f","ddflow/services/metrics/lockgit.py":"100644 73b07c9fadda519e2eb9bbc315fcad5fa3fe5603","ddflow/services/metrics/service.py":"100644 0373a6cde7bf6e7f25bd7a4191504e17ad031193","ddflow/services/perf/suitewaste.py":"100644 aa83641e3801c2f0adc70a17fdc10429fd79d87b","ddflow/surfaces/declared/metrics.py":"100644 f2e36e87ae059d723aedc5f6bdc628c8a2c971f7","ddflow/templates/prompts/help/metrics.md":"100644 19d47d7e9057e9fb05b6e604b943c410fff2da36","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr":"100644 204929c027747c40f99098147d7ed72815d00f22","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr":"100644 7f639cf15068afc43e52713c5a619b30fae5c055","tests/test_suite_waste.py":"100644 767009e6b05f5245adc13a6d56eef9936008f4d6"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba","google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status"